Build a modular 3D astronomical exploration engine using Three.js.

The engine must support rendering and navigation of celestial environments with high visual quality and stable interaction systems.

---

### Core systems

Camera System:

* Smooth, stable, jitter-free camera
* Support free navigation and orbital modes
* Continuous zoom across large distances

Navigation System:

* Free movement in 3D space (X, Y, Z)
* No implicit forces or automatic attraction
* Optional inertia configuration

Celestial Body System:

* Pluggable celestial objects (stars, planets, moons)
* Each body must define:

  * Size
  * Position
  * Rotation
  * Orbit behavior

Rendering System:

* High-quality rendering using Three.js
* Star-based lighting (e.g., Sun as light source)
* Subtle visual effects only (no exaggerated glow or explosions)

Scaling System:

* Handle large spatial scale differences
* Smooth transitions between macro and micro views

---

### Constraints

* The engine must not be hardcoded to a single solar system
* All celestial data must be configurable
* Systems must be modular and decoupled

---

### Non-goals

* No game mechanics
* No scoring or combat
* No arcade-style visuals

---

### Outcome

A reusable engine capable of rendering astronomical environments with smooth navigation and high visual fidelity.
